{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"I removed the stray label that was sending frontend traffic to the search pods, then submitted the mitigation. I haven't confirmed that end-user requests now succeed.\n\n**Root cause:** the `search` deployment's pod template carried the label `service-route: frontend`, which is the `frontend` Service's selector. The `frontend` endpoints therefore included the search pod (`10.244.195.243:5000`), and the search pod doesn't listen on port 5000. Requests routed there would fail.\n\n**Fix:** I removed that label from the `search` deployment template, which rolled a new search pod. `kubectl get ep` then showed `frontend` with only its own pod (`10.244.195.209:5000`) and `search` with `10.244.195.205:8082` and `:9092`.\n\n**Frontend pod:** the frontend pod was replaced (`frontend-d78bbb9f-sjqfb`) during my checks, and I didn't find out why. I didn't investigate further after submitting, so I haven't ruled out something else still changing the deployments."}}
